---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1>ls projects</h1>
    <article>
        <h2>My hackathon projects</h2>
        <p>Four people from my school arranged a team to do czech hackathons. These are our main projects:</p>
        <h3>KompaZ</h3>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/hushkys/kompaz">github</a> - project site is no longer up, infra was too expensive :D</p>
<p>The first app we made, helper in case of a crisis with a chatbot, that can point you to the nearest facility you need.</p>
<p>Won Hackathon of University Hradec Králové 2025, which led us to the national Public Administration Hackathon, which we won in the category of continuing apps.</p>
<p>Techstack: React, Tailwind, Express, PostgreSQL</p>
<h3>KAM</h3>
<p><a href="https://github.com/hushkys/KAM">github</a> - <a href="https://hack-a-ton-hushkys.web.app/">project</a> (in czech)</p>
<p>Region analitical model - draws open data (the theme of the hackathon) to create predictions and see trends in specific areas in the region - for example: aging population in a city, not enough doctors or bus stops, everything in one place.</p>
<p>Won Hackathon of University Hradec Králové 2026, with continuation to the Public Administration office, which will be sometime next year.</p>
<p>Techstack: React, Python, Docker, PostgreSQL</p>
    </article>
  <article>
    <h2>keylog translator</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/damiska21/keylog-translator">github</a> - <a
        href="http://keylog.damiska.xyz/">project</a>  (in czech)
    </p>
    <p>
      A project for me and my local hacking group, translating caught input from
      a keylogger to sensible output without backspaces, arrows and stuff like
      that. Also had the functionality to recognize high-value information from
      the output text like passwords or emails. Never used without consent or outside of training, of
      course.
    </p>
    <p>Techstack: Pure HTML/CSS/JS</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Generic hacking site</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/damiska21/tpw-projekt">github</a> - <a
        href="https://ghs.damiska.xyz">project</a> (half czech, half english)
    </p>
    <p>
      Small, sarcastic site about a hacking group documenting some
      vulnerabilities and their prey >:) Mostly in czech, this was my uni
      assignment.
    </p>
    <p>Techstack: Astro SSG</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Eshop team beta</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/damiska21/eshop-beta">github</a> - <a
        href="https://damiska21.github.io/eshop-beta/">project</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Site to practice React in a team (mine had only 2 people), done in an
      internship. We managed to do every mandatory goals and every complimentary
      goal as well.
    </p>
    <p>Techstack: React, Bootstrap, Tailwind, Fake store api</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
